as we told you just a moment ago we are  just two business days away from the  prospect of another government shutdown  the clock runs out at midnight Thursday  chief congressional correspondent Mike  Emanuel tells us tonight from Capitol  Hill neither Democrats nor Republicans  seem to have the will to make any kind  of long-term commitments the only reason  we do not have a full budget agreement  is because Democrats continue to hold  funding for our government hostage on an  unrelated issue so lawmakers are voting  this week on a fifth continuing  resolution to fund the government from  Thursday night to March 23rd it would  also extend funding for a number of  Medicare pieces and critical public  health programs including community  health centers it's time now to focus on  meeting these essential services  particularly health care and health care  services that are a lifeline Murphy to  win over defense hawks and conservatives  this extension includes increased  funding for the military through the end  of the fiscal year that brought the  conservative house freedom caucus on  board but Democratic leader Chuck  Schumer has declared the house plan dead  on arrival in the Senate holding out for  more domestic spending today the House  Armed Services Committee got an earful  from the Secretary of Defense warning  frequent continuing resolutions and the  existing budget caps are causing the  American military advantage to shrink  the combination of rapidly changing  technology the negative impact on  military readiness resulting from the  longest continuous stretch of combat in  our nation's history and insufficient  funding have created an overstretched  and under-resourced military that may  help the top four congressional leaders  with efforts to get a new long term  funding agreement with more money for  the military and domestic priorities  nearly three hundred billion dollars  more for the next two years which could  get tucked into a short-term extension  I'm optimistic that very soon we'll be  able to reach an agreement I've  discussed some of the outlines with my  caucus that I think  we are very happy with and hopefully the  Republicans are and then we can get  something really good done a budget caps  agreement would make most feel better  about voting for a fifth temporary  government funding extension but more  spending could create new headaches for  GOP leaders when it comes time to raise  the debt ceiling in the coming weeks  Jenna's and it all plays out against the  backdrop of the midterms as well my  Camano on Capitol Hill thank you
 

